My approach:-
1.We need to initialise an list of lists i.e vector<vector<int>> 
2.Create an for loop for creating rows and another for loop for creating elements in the rows
3.Inside the outer for loop i create an row vector of size i+1 and assign value 1
4.Inside the inner for loop we try to add the upper elements and try to over write the row vector elements 
5.Push the row vector after the inner for loop ends
6.repeat untill the number of rows is reached and then return the list of lists 

Time complexity: O(N2)
space complexity: O(N)

My code:
vector<vector<int>> generate(int numRows) {
        vector<vector<int>> v;
        for(int i = 0;i<numRows;i++){
            vector<int> row(i+1,1);
            for(int j = 1;j<i;j++){
                row[j] = v[i-1][j-1] + v[i-1][j] ;
            }
            v.push_back(row);
        }
        return v;
    }
